## Bookmarks vs Read Later

Cardmaniacs separates **intent**:

| | Read Later | Bookmarks |
|---|------------|-----------|
| **Intent** | Read soon / working through | Keep for reference |
| **Shortcut** | `⌘2` | `⌘3` |
| **Sidebar mode** | `⌘⌥L` | `⌘⌥B` |
| **Mental model** | Queue | Library shelf |

A documentation page you will revisit for months belongs in **Bookmarks**. A long article you want to finish this week belongs in **Read Later**.

Both use the same card, reader, tags, and highlights—only organization and sidebar collections differ.

## Adding bookmarks

- **Quick Add** (`⌘N`) — paste URL, choose bookmark destination when prompted
- **Share extension** — save from Safari, News, or other apps
- **Save from feeds** — palette actions when you want reference, not queue
- **Drag URL** — onto Cardmaniacs on macOS where supported

## Collections

Bookmarks sidebar destinations include:

- **All bookmarks** (folder tree)
- **Starred Bookmarks** — palette: Go to Starred Bookmarks
- **Archived Bookmarks** — palette: Go to Archived Bookmarks
- **Unread Bookmarks** — palette: Go to Unread Bookmarks

User-created **folders** nest under Bookmarks in the sidebar. Drag cards between folders or use **Move…** (`⌘⇧M`).

## Starring and tags

- **Toggle Star** (`⌘⇧S`) highlights important bookmarks within a folder
- **Manage Tags…** (`⌘⇧T`) applies cross-library labels—useful for “tools”, “recipes”, “work”

Smart lists can surface bookmarks matching tag and source rules alongside feed and queue items. See [Highlights and Tags](/docs/highlights-and-tags).

## Read states

Bookmarks can be unread (not yet opened in Cardmaniacs) or read. **Unread Bookmarks** helps you process saved links you have not reviewed in the app—distinct from Read Later’s In Progress.

Mark read with `⌘E` when you have reviewed the page in the reader.

## Archive and delete

- **Archive** (palette) — remove from active folders, recoverable from Archived Bookmarks
- **Delete** (`⌘⌫`) — permanent removal

Prefer archive when unsure.

## Opening externally

**Open in Browser** (`⌘⌥O`) launches the live site—useful when the bookmarked page changes frequently and reader extraction is not the source of truth.

**Copy Link** (`⌘⇧C`) shares the URL without leaving Cardmaniacs.

## Capture from other apps

Configure the Share extension under **Settings → General**. Safari extension actions may offer “bookmark” vs “read later” when saving.

Handoff and Spotlight (see [AI and Integrations](/docs/ai-and-integrations)) can resume bookmarked or recent items across devices.

